cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "Critic Architecture Matters: Dual vs. Unified Critics for Humanoid Loco-Manipulation"
abstract: >-
  Official implementation of the paper, which compares dual and unified critic
  architectures for multi-objective humanoid loco-manipulation on the Unitree G1 in
  NVIDIA Isaac Lab, training policies through sequential curricula that progress from
  stationary reaching to walking with variable-orientation targets. The two runs differ
  in more than the critic (curriculum, locomotion reward weight, arm action
  dimensionality, one seed each), so the measured gap is reported as a relation between
  two runs rather than a causal effect of the critic; see the Confounding Factors section
  of the paper (v2).
